+# H2 source-driven feature workflow
+
+Use this workflow for H2 FSGen source-to-native CAD. It is an **agent skill using
+normal Browser controls, deterministic H2 CLI commands, and the existing Native
+MCP/session bridge**. It is not a single autonomous MCP call. Individual source
+features have live proofs; a complete generated car and assemblies remain
+separate acceptance gates. Do not infer full acceptance from installed commands.
+
+For H2, these instructions override the general skill's REST fallback: no REST
+CAD writes, canvas modeling, guessed RPCs, copied sample IDs, or alternative
+targets. The Browser step allocates or selects ordinary features; the CLI
+generates their geometry from source.
+
+## Establish source, runtime, and target
+
+1. Use the existing compatible H2 Python environment and Native MCP launcher.
+   Inspect `python -m h2cad --help` if command discovery is needed. The bridge
+   config must pin the approved test Part Studio and existing SQLite journal.
+   Keep private configuration, pairing material, model readbacks, and journal
+   files out of the plugin package and published source.
+2. Resolve the exact document/workspace/element URL and connected editor tab.
+   Use `bridge_status`, `native_state`, and `editor_tab` from the existing MCP
+   server for inspection. Use the official Browser plugin for trusted UI input,
+   with controls discovered from the current DOM. A new tab ID is not a new
+   target. Do not change the configured target to bypass a refusal.
+3. Run both local commands before modeling:
+
+   ```text
+   python -m h2cad compile SOURCE --did DID --wid WID --eid EID --output desired.json
+   python -m h2cad validate SOURCE
+   ```
+
+   Require successful local geometry validation. Review the compiled snapshot's
+   feature list and dependencies against supported operations below. Stop on
+   unsupported source semantics; do not substitute imported or opaque geometry.
+4. Check the actual loaded server/page capabilities. The required pairs are
+   `h2_native_variable_populate_server_v1` / `h2_native_variable_populate_page_v1`,
+   `h2_native_plane_populate_server_v1` / `h2_native_plane_populate_page_v1`,
+   `h2_source_sketch_server_v1` / `h2_source_sketch_page_v1`, and
+   `h2_source_extrude_server_v1` / `h2_source_extrude_page_v1`.
+   A source checkout or staged extension is not evidence of an active runtime.
+
+## Consume the compiled feature order
+
+Iterate the compiled snapshot's `features` in order, retaining its logical IDs
+and source expressions. Maintain the small operation-ID binding map needed for
+the CLI inputs; the existing journal remains authoritative. Bind each source
+logical ID to its observed operation and native feature ID. Use original source
+and the same pinned journal throughout. Do not reorder all planes or sketches
+into separate batches, use displayed names as identity, or allocate a duplicate
+feature to work around an uncertain operation.
+
+Before each normal UI allocation, read the exact saved-idle native state. For
+commands requiring `--baseline`, save the complete JSON state returned by
+`python -m h2cad inspect --did DID --wid WID --eid EID --bridge-config CONFIG --tab-id TAB`.
+Its `target`, `connected`, `editingFeatureId`, `element_microversion`, and full
+`tree` must be retained. Capture it **before** opening the next draft, not after.
+
+Each population command has this common form:
+
+```text
+python -m h2cad COMMAND SOURCE --logical-id "SOURCE_LOGICAL_ID" --did DID --wid WID --eid EID --bridge-config CONFIG --tab-id TAB --journal JOURNAL ADDITIONAL_ARGUMENTS
+```
+
+| Source operation | Normal Browser step | Command and additional arguments |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Literal ASSIGNED/LENGTH variable | Open one new unnamed Variable draft, LENGTH type, zero default length | `experimental-populate-variable`; repeat `--previous-variable-op-id OP` for every preceding observed source variable, in order |
+| Supported OFFSET plane | Open one normal Plane draft and select its exact observed reference plane; leave other native defaults | `experimental-populate-plane --baseline BASELINE.json --reference-binding BINDING.json --variable-operations VARS.json`; repeat `--previous-plane-op-id OP` for preceding observed source planes |
+| Supported rectangle or circle sketch | Open one blank normal Sketch and select the exact source plane from its observed operation | `experimental-populate-source-sketch --baseline BASELINE.json --plane-op-id PLANE_OP --variable-operations VARS.json` |
+| NEW/SOLID/BLIND extrusion | Select the exact saved source sketch row, open Extrude, verify whole-sketch region binding and NEW mode; retain literal draft depth | `experimental-populate-source-extrusion --baseline BASELINE.json --sketch-op-id SKETCH_OP`; add `--variable-op-id VARIABLE_OP` for a direct source variable depth |
+
+For the first variable or plane, omit the corresponding previous-operation
+flags. Subsequent flags contain all prior operations of that kind in source
+order, not only the immediately preceding one. `VARS.json` is an object mapping
+exact source dependency names to observed variable operation IDs, for example
+`{"#length":"OBSERVED_LENGTH_OP","#width":"OBSERVED_WIDTH_OP"}`. Supply only the
+dependencies required by that plane/sketch, or `{}` when there are none.
+
+For a plane, `BINDING.json` contains `target`, `element_microversion`, `query`, and
+`query_data`. Read `query` from the active plane's sole `entities` query. Resolve
+it with the existing read-only MCP `native_read` and the supported
+`ui.GBTUiGetQueryDataCall`, using that query unchanged. `query_data` is the exact
+single returned query-data item; `target` and revision come from that active
+draft state. Recheck that the state is unchanged. Never synthesize deterministic
+IDs or fill the file from a previous studio's sample. Sketch/extrusion commands
+perform their own query resolution and do not take this plane binding file.
+
+For the basic car, the compiled source starts with seven variables, then
+`Chassis height` → `Chassis sketch` → `Chassis`, followed by its remaining source
+dependencies. This is an example, not a hardcoded execution schedule. The
+Chassis sketch uses the observed plane operation and `#length`/`#width` variable
+operations; Chassis uses the observed sketch operation and source depth `8 mm`.
+Later symbolic extrusions retain their `#bodyHeight` or `#wheelThickness`
+expressions rather than substituting the evaluated number.
+
+## Require proof before advancing
+
+The CLI records intent before a possible write. Native serializer constructors
+allocate new node IDs; normal UI allocation owns feature IDs. The writer preserves
+existing native identities, full source expressions, and unrelated feature data.
+Sketches use a local fixed origin point. Every constrained point and circle
+radius must match the active solver graph before Commit. Opposite-sign alignment
+may be an explicitly inferred candidate; solver failure is not permission to
+retry with another sign. Independent saved readback must still verify the source
+definition and generated identities.
+
+Advance only when the exact operation is journaled `observed`, saved-idle state
+is independently confirmed, and marker retirement/readiness is confirmed. An RPC
+acknowledgement or the receipt fields `normal_ui_save_invoked` and legacy
+`normal_ui_finish` describe invocation only. `completion_pending` is not failure
+to create and is not a retry instruction.
+
+| Original operation | Reconciliation command |
+| --- | --- |
+| Variable | `experimental-reconcile-saved-source-variable` |
+| Plane | `experimental-reconcile-saved-source-plane` |
+| Source sketch | `experimental-reconcile-saved-source-sketch` |
+| Source extrusion | `experimental-reconcile-saved-source-extrude` |
+
+```text
+python -m h2cad RECONCILIATION_COMMAND OP_ID --bridge-config CONFIG --tab-id TAB --journal JOURNAL
+```
+
+Reconciliation reads CAD state and updates the matching journal/marker only
+after positive proof. It never replays geometry. If normal Save completion is
+pending, inspect the exact draft and use normal controls only when appropriate.
+A fresh same-target tab may independently show saved state when the original
+controller is stale. Preserve the original pending operation and draft; do not
+cancel it, overwrite it, or clear a guard by assumption. Missing solver receipts,
+changed source/target, unresolved writes, different definitions, or a mismatched
+marker keep the workflow stopped. A proven pre-dispatch rejection means no
+modeling command was sent, but still inspect and preserve the existing draft.
+
+After source feature creation, independently check final solids, bounds and an
+ordinary parameter edit that regenerates dependent geometry. Restore the
+intended parameter value and recheck identities and definitions. Saved feature
+proof is not complete-car, assembly, or mechanical-design acceptance.
